{
  "abstract": "This project proves the Reinhardt conjecture in Lean 4. Every centrally symmetric convex disk in the plane has greatest packing density at least that of the smoothed octagon, approximately 0.902414. The smoothed octagon is a regular octagon whose corners are replaced by arcs of hyperbolas. Equality holds precisely for its images under invertible affine maps.\n\nThe proof uses Hales's optimal control formulation and builds on the libraries lean4-smoothed-polygon and lean4-optimal-control. It also verifies the construction and packing density of the smoothed octagon.",
